# ─── Palawan Site Engine — environment variables ────────────────────────────
# Every variable used by the repo must be listed here. Copy to .env.local
# (or .env for local dev). Never commit real secrets.
#
# Phase 0: no runtime secrets required yet. The variables below are
# reserved for later phases and are documented now so they are not
# introduced ad-hoc.

# ── Next.js ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL      Public base URL of the rendered site (apps/web).
#                           Default in dev: http://localhost:3000
# NEXT_PUBLIC_STUDIO_URL    Public base URL of the agency studio (apps/studio).
#                           Default in dev: http://localhost:3001

# ── Database (Phase 2: Payload CMS + PostgreSQL) ───────────────────────────
# DATABASE_URL              Postgres connection string, e.g.
#                           postgres://user:password@localhost:5432/palawan_site_engine
# PAYLOAD_SECRET            Long random secret for Payload auth/sessions (>=32 chars).
#                           Generate: openssl rand -hex 32

# ── Media storage (Phase 2) ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# S3_ENDPOINT               S3-compatible endpoint (e.g. Cloudflare R2: https://<accountId>.r2.cloudflarestorage.com)
# S3_BUCKET                 Bucket name for tenant media.
# S3_REGION                 Bucket region (e.g. auto for R2).
# S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID          Access key ID. Server-only; never prefixed with NEXT_PUBLIC_.
# S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY      Secret access key. Server-only.
# S3_PUBLIC_URL             Base URL for public media (optional; private media uses signed URLs).

# ── Auth / rate limiting (Phase 2+) ────────────────────────────────────────
# AUTH_RATE_LIMIT_WINDOW_MS Window for auth rate limiting (default 900000 = 15 min).
# AUTH_RATE_LIMIT_MAX       Max attempts per window per IP (default 10).

# ── Email (Phase 3: inquiry / booking notifications) ───────────────────────
# MAIL_FROM                 Sender address, e.g. noreply@example.test
# SMTP_HOST                 SMTP host (omit to use console adapter in dev).
# SMTP_PORT                 SMTP port (default 587).
# SMTP_USER                 SMTP user (server-only).
# SMTP_PASS                 SMTP password (server-only).
# RESEND_API_KEY            Resend API key if using Resend adapter (server-only).

# ── Deployment (Phase 5) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# VERCEL_TOKEN              Vercel API token for the VercelProvider (server-only).
# VERCEL_TEAM_ID            Vercel team ID (optional).
# DEPLOY_PROVIDER           Deployment provider selection: "vercel" | "local-docker" (default: vercel).

# ── Hermes integration (Phase 6) ───────────────────────────────────────────
# HERMES_API_KEY_<AGENCY>   Per-agency API key for /api/hermes routes (server-only, scoped, rate limited, audit-logged).
# HERMES_PREVIEW_SECRET     Secret for signing expiring preview tokens (server-only).
